# Emby SSO licence service - example configuration
#
#   cp service/.env.example service/.env
#   chmod 600 service/.env
#   # fill in the blanks, then:
#   docker compose up -d --build licence
#
# The values below are the ones a real first run on a real host was verified
# with, except the secrets, which are blank. See docs/first-run.md.
#
# NEVER COMMIT THE .env YOU MAKE FROM THIS. It is gitignored; keep it that way.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Inside the container. The host file it is mounted from must be owned by uid
# 5678 and mode 600, or the service refuses to start. docs/first-run.md step 3.
LICENCE_SIGNING_KEY_PATH=/run/secrets/licence-signing-key.private.json

# Inside the container, on the mounted volume. Holds the SQLite store, the
# ledger of who bought what, and the outbox. BACK IT UP.
LICENCE_DATA_DIR=/data

# The address the PLUGIN has compiled in. If these disagree, buy links point
# nowhere and activation fails. Note the spelling: license, not licence.
LICENCE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://license.koper.cloud

# sandbox until a real purchase has been tested end to end.
PAYPAL_ENV=sandbox

# From the PayPal developer dashboard, on the webhook you created. PayPal signs
# it into every message, so a wrong value fails every webhook CLOSED - which is
# the safe direction, and also means "nothing happens" is the symptom.
PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required to actually sell. Without them the service still runs and codes can
# still be issued by hand; /buy just says "not set up to take payments yet".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=

PAYPAL_CURRENCY=EUR
PAYPAL_PRICE=19.00

# The floor a captured payment must clear. Defaults to PAYPAL_PRICE, so set it
# only to allow something lower deliberately. It exists because without a floor
# a captured payment of any size - a penny - would buy a full licence.
# PAYPAL_MINIMUM_AMOUNT=19.00

# PAYPAL_PRODUCT_NAME=Emby SSO plugin licence
# PAYPAL_RETURN_URL=       # defaults to LICENCE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL/buy/complete
# PAYPAL_CANCEL_URL=       # defaults to LICENCE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL/buy/cancelled

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licence shape (defaults shown)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# How many DIFFERENT Emby servers one code may be activated onto. Re-activating
# onto a server it already holds is free and does not count.
# LICENCE_ACTIVATIONS_ALLOWED=3

# How long an issued licence lasts. There is NO REVOCATION - the plugin checks
# offline and never calls home - so this is the only control you have over a
# licence once it exists. Choose deliberately.
# LICENCE_DAYS=365

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rate limiting on /v1/activate (defaults shown)
#
# Redemption codes are bearer secrets guessed over the internet and this
# endpoint cannot be authenticated, so this is the brake. A real user activates
# once; these numbers only bite a script.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# LICENCE_RATE_PER_CLIENT_PER_MINUTE=10
# LICENCE_RATE_PER_CLIENT_BURST=5
# LICENCE_RATE_GLOBAL_PER_MINUTE=300
# LICENCE_RATE_MAX_TRACKED_CLIENTS=20000

# How many reverse proxies sit in front of this service. 0 means the socket's
# peer address IS the client. Set it WRONG-HIGH and a caller can spoof their own
# address through X-Forwarded-For and walk around the rate limit above.
# LICENCE_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Emailing the code. ALL OPTIONAL - off unless SMTP_HOST is set.
#
# Off is a working configuration: paid codes land in /data/codes-outbox.jsonl
# and you send them by hand. A failed send NEVER fails the webhook.
# See docs/email-delivery-checklist.md before trusting a real send.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_FROM_ADDRESS=licences@example.com
# SMTP_USERNAME=licences@example.com
# SMTP_PASSWORD=

# One of exactly three words:
#   tls        implicit TLS, encrypted from the first byte, usually port 465
#   starttls   plain then MUST upgrade, fails rather than continuing in the
#              clear, usually 587. THE DEFAULT.
#   none       no encryption. Only for a relay on this host. Setting a username
#              with this refuses to start, because that puts the relay password
#              on the wire.
# SMTP_SECURITY=starttls
# SMTP_PORT=587            # defaults to 465/587/25 to match SMTP_SECURITY

# SMTP_FROM_NAME=Emby SSO licences
# SMTP_REPLY_TO=help@example.com
# SMTP_SUBJECT=Your Emby SSO plugin licence code
# SMTP_SUPPORT_CONTACT=help@example.com
# SMTP_TEMPLATE_PATH=/run/config/licence-email.txt   # must contain {code}
# SMTP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
# SMTP_MAX_ATTEMPTS=4      # then the outbox is the fallback
# SMTP_RETRY_SECONDS=30    # first backoff, quadrupled each attempt
